   "texts": [
    "Even the Moon has wrinkles.",
    "The research team counted more than 8,900.",
    "It looks smooth in the night sky.",
    "Up close, though, it seems to have many “wrinkles.”",
    "But it does not need beauty cream.",
    "These wrinkles give clues about how the Moon became smaller.",
    "They also hint at its surprising way of “dressing.”",
    "The team used pictures from the Moon probe LRO.",
    "They looked for cliffs on the Moon’s surface and marked them on a map.",
    "A wrinkle is a cliff with one steep side and one less steep side.",
    "Scientists think these cliffs show where solid rock was squeezed together.",
    "One side was pushed up over the other.",
    "The cliffs are a record of a huge “shoving match” cut into the Moon’s surface.",
    "Using the map, the team worked out how much the Moon had shrunk.",
    "They estimated that its radius had become about 42 to 46 meters smaller.",
    "By reading the wrinkles on its surface, scientists are studying how a huge object in space became smaller.",
    "Measuring the Moon is a very detailed job."
   ]
  },
