   "texts": [
    "But you may be thinking, “Has the Moon shrunk only that much since it formed?”",
    "Wait a moment.",
    "The shrinkage we can see comes from the later part of the Moon’s history.",
    "It was left by faults that formed fairly recently.",
    "This is not the full amount of shrinking from its birth to today.",
    "On the other hand, models of the Moon’s cooling over all its history predict much more shrinking.",
    "Does that mean the models are very wrong?",
    "It is too soon to know.",
    "The time periods are different.",
    "The studies also used different methods.",
    "These numbers were not measured under the same conditions.",
    "Still, the difference is puzzling.",
    "One possible answer is a layer of broken rock.",
    "It is like a “rock coat” that the Moon has put on.",
    "Just hearing this may make your shoulders ache.",
    "But its weight is not what matters.",
    "What matters is how well it holds heat in."
   ]
  },
