   "texts": [
    "The team thinks a thick layer of rock with many gaps may have worked like insulation.",
    "Insulation in a house keeps heat from getting out.",
    "This rock layer may have made it harder for heat inside the Moon to get out.",
    "So the Moon may have cooled and shrunk more slowly.",
    "In other words, the Moon may have stayed warm inside its rock coat.",
    "But it is too soon to solve the mystery by saying, “The coat is to blame!”",
    "For now, it is only one possible reason for the difference.",
    "Counting cliffs on the Moon led to questions about its inner heat.",
    "Then came the warmth of its coat—not how it feels to wear, but how well it holds heat in.",
    "The wrinkles were an important clue to how the Moon cooled.",
    "Next time you look up at the Moon, imagine the “rock coat” beneath its round shape, too.",
    "There is more to the Moon’s way of dressing than you can see."
   ]
